@*
    A wrestler, as something you can recognise without reading.

    There is no photography in this game and licensing real likenesses is not a thing a
    hobby project does, so this is the honest substitute: initials, on a ground coloured by
    alignment, at a consistent size everywhere a name appears. A review put the problem
    plainly — seventy-six wrestlers and not one face, so scanning the roster is reading
    rather than looking, and the rows are told apart only by the alignment badge's colour.

    Two initials, not one, which is not uniqueness and is not meant to be — Roman Reigns and
    Rhea Ripley are both RR on this roster. It is a shape to scan by, next to the name that
    actually identifies them: one letter collides constantly enough to be useless for that,
    and two rarely enough to be worth drawing.

    The colour is alignment rather than per-wrestler, because a random hue per name is
    decoration and alignment is the thing a booker is actually scanning for — the picker is
    mostly a search for someone to work against the person already in the match.
*@
<span class="portrait portrait--@Tone @(Size is null ? "" : $"portrait--{Size}") @Class"
      aria-hidden="true" title="@Wrestler.RingName">@Initials</span>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public Wrestler Wrestler { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>"sm" in dense rows, null at the default size, "lg" for a lineup slot.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Size { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Placement class from the caller, so the grid area lives with the grid.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Class { get; set; }

    private string Tone => Wrestler.Gimmick?.NaturalAlignment switch
    {
        Alignment.Face => "face",
        Alignment.Heel => "heel",
        _              => "tweener"
    };

    /// <summary>
    /// Up to two initials from the ring name. Single-word names keep their first two letters
    /// — "Asuka" is AS rather than A — because one letter collides constantly and a blank
    /// second slot looks like a rendering fault.
    /// </summary>
    private string Initials
    {
        get
        {
            var words = Wrestler.RingName
                .Split(' ', StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries | StringSplitOptions.TrimEntries)
                .Where(w => char.IsLetter(w[0]))
                .ToList();

            return words.Count switch
            {
                0 => "?",
                1 => words[0].Length > 1 ? words[0][..2].ToUpperInvariant()
                                         : words[0].ToUpperInvariant(),
                _ => $"{words[0][0]}{words[^1][0]}".ToUpperInvariant()
            };
        }
    }
}
